        <td bgcolor="whitesmoke" colspan="2" valign="top">
		<img src="icon_mi_1.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;04/06/2005&nbsp;:&nbsp; 13:01:18</font>

		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=4"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
 
			&nbsp;<a href="JavaScript:openWindow('pop_mail.asp?id=4')"><img src="icon_email.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Email Poster" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

				&nbsp;<a href="privatesend.asp?method=Topic&mname=Kaashar"><img src="pm.gif" width="11" height="17" alt="Send Kaashar a Private Message" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        &nbsp;<a href="JavaScript:openWindow('pop_messengers.asp?mode=ICQ&ICQ=749934&M_NAME=Kaashar')"><img src="http://online.mirabilis.com/scripts/online.dll?icq=749934&img=5" height=15 width=15 alt="Send Kaashar an ICQ Message" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?ARCHIVE=&method=TopicQuote&TOPIC_ID=8298&FORUM_ID=27&CAT_ID=6&Forum_Title=World+of+Warcraft&Topic_Title=Kaashar%27s+Big+Group+PvP+101"><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
<font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> More people are joining us in our Southshore PvP excursions, so I thought I'd post a few tips I've learned along the way.</P><P><ul><BR><li>Unless you're a rogue, stay with the group.  Mages can instantly blink forward from where they are, they'll blink and sheep you if you're away from the pack.   Enemy rogues are ALWAYS out there, stay near the hunter that's throwing flares.  </li><BR><li>Night elves learn to shadowmeld...a lot.  It prevents enemies from making you a target at a distance, to sheep, aimshot, etc.   It also helps hide your group's numbers.  </li><BR><li>With few exceptions, you aren't going to solo an opposing player.  This isn't a_dumb_npc99.  Watch your surroundings, if you see somebody else engage a target be aware of the enemy presence around their target.   Sometimes it's better to take a member of the opposing team out of commission (sheep, sap, etc) before assisting on the kill.  99% of the time both players are so engaged in their respective fights they lose combat awareness. </li><BR><li>Hunters, throw flares, lay traps, CONSTANTLY!  Learn to use eyes of the beast as a targeting/pet positioning tool.  Be aware of your enemy and what they are capable of to lay the apropriate trap (Rogues/warriors you'll want freeze ; mages/priests generally you'll want frost, etc).  HOTKEY Viper sting and concussion shot, they are your most powerful PvP weapons.<BR>*Serpent Sting Warriors<BR>*Scorpid Sting Rogues/hunters<BR>*Viper Sting shaman/priests/mages/warlocks/druids</P><P><li> Druids & Shaman in animal form are considered animals.  Hunters can fear them, Druids can mez them.  If you see a druid in animal form and you're one of those two classes...laugh at the poor idiot feral druid and kill 'em.</li></P><P><li>See that level 60 with the blue name while your own is green?  Expect his flagging move to be attacking you.  Bank on it, trust me (as a side note, please don't do that if you're an Arbiter, I like to think of us as more honorable than that)</li></P><P>[*]If you're fighting a mage on open ground, get some low level critter to agro you before engagement.  That level 20 bear doing 1 point of damage will save your butt when you get sheep'd.</li><BR></ul></P><P>Edited by - kaashar on 04/06/2005  13:01:52</font> 

</td>
</tr>

