		<font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><b>Wolflad</a>
        </b></font>

        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>Arbiter Member</small></font>

		<br><img src="http://www.webwolves.org/misc_graphics/avatar.gif" alt="Wolflad" width="60" height="60" border=0 hspace="2" vspace="2">
		
        <br>
        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>USA</small></font>
        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>1156 Posts</small></font></td>
        <td bgcolor="whitesmoke" colspan="2" valign="top">
		<a name="50615"></a>
		<img src="icon_mi_1.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;04/06/2005&nbsp;:&nbsp; 14:07:54</font>

		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=39"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
			&nbsp;<a href="JavaScript:openWindow('pop_mail.asp?id=39')"><img src="icon_email.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Email Poster" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

				&nbsp;<a href="privatesend.asp?method=Topic&mname=Wolflad"><img src="pm.gif" width="11" height="17" alt="Send Wolflad a Private Message" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        &nbsp;<a href="http://www.webwolves.org/ryan/" target="_blank"><img src="icon_homepage.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Visit Wolflad's Homepage" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?ARCHIVE=&method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=50615&TOPIC_ID=8298&FORUM_ID=27&CAT_ID=6&Forum_Title=World+of+Warcraft&Topic_Title=Kaashar%27s+Big+Group+PvP+101&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> <BR>My 2 cents as a druid:</P><P></P><P></P><P></P><P></P><P></P><P></P><P></P><P> <ul><li>Rooting / mezzing enemies in combat is useless, since they wake up instantly. Rooting a fleeing enemy being pursued by guards or players is teh win though.</li><li>Faerie Fire rogues when you see them, it keeps them from re-stealthing.</li><li>Always fight with buffs on.</li><li>Look at the clock when you die; it's often better to wait 5 min. and let your flag expire before rezzing so you don't get rogue-ganked immediately when you respawn.</li><li>If the Tarren Mill guards get spawned by idiots, expect a horde rush to accompany the guard zerg.  </li><li>Never leave your groupmates. =)  </li><li> If the day of the week ends with a 'Y', there's stealthed rogues around. </li></ul></P><P><img src="http://www.webwolves.org/misc_graphics/nesig.png" border=0><a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

      <tr>
        <td bgcolor="gainsboro" valign="top">

		<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=223">
	
		<font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><b>Blackedge</a>
        </b></font>

        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>Guest</small></font>

        <br>
        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>USA</small></font>
        <br><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1"><small>387 Posts</small></font></td>
        <td bgcolor="gainsboro" colspan="2" valign="top">
		<a name="50619"></a>
		<img src="icon_mi_1.gif" border="0" hspace="3"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="1">Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;04/07/2005&nbsp;:&nbsp; 09:11:43</font>

		&nbsp;<a href="pop_profile.asp?mode=display&id=223"><img src="icon_profile.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Show Profile" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>
        
			&nbsp;<a href="JavaScript:openWindow('pop_mail.asp?id=223')"><img src="icon_email.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Email Poster" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

				&nbsp;<a href="privatesend.asp?method=Topic&mname=Blackedge"><img src="pm.gif" width="11" height="17" alt="Send Blackedge a Private Message" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?ARCHIVE=&method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=50619&TOPIC_ID=8298&FORUM_ID=27&CAT_ID=6&Forum_Title=World+of+Warcraft&Topic_Title=Kaashar%27s+Big+Group+PvP+101&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Being on the Horde side of these battles, I would like to give my perspective about the guard situation.   Guards at <b>both</b> towns can zerg equally.  What makes the TM guards seem so much worse is guard spawn seems to depend on (How many NPC's you agro/How far into town you have progressed).<BR>TM is an outhouse compared to SS size wise.  10 feet into TM is the equivalent of almost a building and a half for SS.  We pushed into SS last night, all the way tot he docks.  Outcome?  I was finally brought down by no less that 20 SS guards.....in the TM GRAVEYARD! <img src=icon_smile_blackeye.gif border=0 align=middle><img src=icon_smile_angry.gif border=0 align=middle>  The SS guards almost cleared 1/2 the TM guards before we brought them all down.  On my server, the horde rarely pushes into SS to avoid the guard spam.  We can sit peacefully on the hill right outside without triggering the "enemy in town" spam.  We are there to pvp, not fight guard zerg.  We get kinda cranky when the Alliance are being mean though <img src=icon_smile_wink.gif border=0 align=middle></P><P>As for tips:<BR><ul><li>No matter the size of your party, look behind you every 10-30 sec.  Always a very good chance a rogue is having his way with the very back person and no one has noticed.  </li><li>As much as I hate saying this as a warlock, if you see one, kill the pet first.   Right now, the best way to take a warlock out of any fight is to eat up all his soul shards.  Also, never assume a warlock is an easy kill.   While it is true that most of them suck, and suck hard, a good one can hand you your rear before you realise what happened.   Ask any of the 5 or so rogues that jumped me last night.(not all at once, although I have survived a double team from rogues before.<BR>  </li><li>Mass of enemy standing outside your town?   Got at least half their number?  Do they appear not to be a well tuned raid?  <b>Charge.</b> Everyone at once just run at them.  All it takes is one of them turning to flee and its a pack effect.   Not once have I seen a raid stand its ground if charged by a force at least half its size or bigger.  The simple motion of the hunters backpedaling to keep range will unnerve the rest of the people, making them back up as well, which makes the hunters back up further.  Its a domino effect and really really hard to resist.  </li> <li> Pesky level 60 folks terrorizing your newb area?  Lots of guards around?  Are you a hunter or warlock?  Time to be the general.   Guards are not a very motivated bunch, and have the eye sight of mole with sunglasses on.  They stand around just waiting to be told what to do.  Thats where YOU come in.  Most 60's have a pretty good idea where to stand to avoid guard agro.  Most 60's can kill a couple guards.   When it gets to be 3+ though is where its fun, and thats your job.   See, guards have union rules, and get nice breaks and all.  But part of the deal is, they have to <b>SEE</b> you in trouble before they will lift a finger.  WoW is programed so that for agro/combat purposes, your pet and you are in/out of combat together.  Send fluffy out and lean on said guard.   Soon as your pet attacks, it puts you in combat, and you are in trouble.   Since you are standing on top of the guards, they HAVE to help you.  And will do so gladly.  Assisting your pet on whatever it is attacking.  <3 the bewildered reaction of people as they get swarmed by 10 + guards well outside the normal agro range. </li></ul></P><P></P><P>Blackedge Shadowbringer:<BR>65 Dread Lord of Bertoxxulous<BR><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=25967" target="_blank">http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=25967</a></P><P>Bearpaw:<BR>60 Warlock of Syzygy<BR>Lothar Server</P><P>Edited by - Blackedge on 04/07/2005  10:22:05</P><P>Edited by - Blackedge on 04/07/2005  10:29:12<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" al