        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Up until wednesday I was a Soul Link demonologist, also specced for Hellfire. Soulfire is good in pvp but i was mostly spamming Shadowbolt. I had a bad day on wednesday dieing all the time mostly thru alck of situational awareness. I respecced on Wednesday to Destruction and searing pain so that I could nuke faster. I also re-arranged my hotkeys to dot easier. <BR>Friday I think I did a good job, still died but I saw at least 5 kills go down either under nukes by me or dots as they ran so I was happy. </P><P>What I want to do sometime is test something. I was using curse of elements yesterday and hoping the damage boost to my nukes, dots and imp were more costly to them then Curse of Agony. CoA is very back loaded doing something like 10/30/60% damage in each third of its 30 second life. Total damage is 1095. So I<BR>am just wondering if the Coe works better then CoA. The other thing is that Vrish is a shadow priest, and at least some of the Hunters shots are arcane based, so I think I'm gonna test using curse of shadow instead to see if that helps more. Now gotta go farm another 42 shards for todays pvp. :-)</P><P><BR><a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
